REPLACE THIS FILE with your chosen license text before running bootstrap.sh:

    curl -fsSL https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.txt -o LICENSE

bootstrap.sh only checks that this file exists and is non-empty. It does not
verify the contents — putting the right text here is your decision, and a
string check would only pretend to be a verification.

The first commit must not depend on whether the network was up, which is why
the license is a checked-in artifact rather than something fetched at run time.

MIT is a fine alternative. Apache-2.0 is the default here for its express
patent grant, which is what lets someone at a company contribute without
asking legal first.
